THINK need rigid_frame: Structure that keeps everything at the right distance. Not a moving mechanism, but every mechanism depends on it. Rules: A joint with one pin can swing: use two pins, an axle in cross holes, or close a triangle/rectangle. Shafts' bearings must sit in the frame at the gear spacing.
THINK why The elbow bracket has only one round hole and one cross hole; a friction peg in each turns those into two usable mounting studs at right angles, so the beam and the frame's bottom corner can both attach here later.
THINK role bracket-L in the frame / housing: Left corner post: anchors pin-blue-A (holds the beam) and pin-red-A (unused stub in this 11-step booklet).
THINK role pin-blue-A in the frame / housing: Carries beam-C's left end.
THINK role pin-red-A in the frame / housing: Free stub on the left corner; not reached again in this booklet.
