THINK need gear_pair: Passes turning from one parallel shaft to another. Changes speed and force by the tooth ratio and reverses direction. Rules: Gears must be locked to their shafts (cross hole on axle). Shafts must turn freely (round holes) and be held at the right distance: (teeth_a + teeth_b) / 16 holes for spur gears (e.g. 16+16 = 2 holes, 8+24 = 2, 12+20 = 2). Each shaft needs support on two points or the gears push apart.
THINK need shaft_with_stops: An axle that carries parts and turns, held from sliding by stops at both ends. Rules: At least two round-hole bearings. A stop on each side of the bearings.
THINK why gear-gray-L and gear-tan-M are locked to the shaft (cross-hole gears) so they always turn with it; bush-K keeps the shaft from sliding left; fork-R's round hole lets the shaft spin free on the right.
THINK role bush-K in the gear shaft and clutch: Spacer/stop near the main shaft's left end, locked to axle-N.
THINK role gear-gray-L in the gear shaft and clutch: Gear locked to axle-N; meshes with the input gear gear-blue-U.
THINK role gear-tan-M in the gear shaft and clutch: Gear locked to axle-N near the output end; always turns with the main shaft.
THINK role axle-N in the gear shaft and clutch: The main shaft: carries bush-K, gear-gray-L, the clutch sleeve, gear-red-P (free) and gear-tan-M, and exits through fork-R and ext-W as the output.
